Subject: [PATCH 32/68] Sync the liveness engine: engine commit 9bf9e83
 (Mosip26 history cleanup)

Before its first push, Mosip26's unpublished history was rewritten to
leave out large model files that were later replaced (fix round 3), so
every commit there has a new hash. The engine sources, the models and
the camera source are unchanged:
- engine-sync.txt names the engine commit by its new hash, 9bf9e83
  ("F1: int8 SFace, signed bundle pad-2026.10.5"; 3eea3dc before);
- the four jars are rebuilt at Mosip26 5c59a60, so their git.properties
  name a published commit. The jars synced before named 81c528c, a commit
  the rewrite dropped. Only git.properties differs inside the jars, so
  only their SHA-256 lines change;
- the models and CameraXFrameSource.java have the same SHA-256 as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
